// Calls the API made out to Azure SQL.
//
// This is the query worth showing. Request telemetry only proves the web tier answered;
// dependency telemetry proves the call reached through to the database and came back, and it
// attributes the time between the two tiers. When a request is slow, this is what says whether
// the API was slow or the database was.
//
// Expect the first row after an idle period to be dramatically slower than the rest: that is the
// serverless database resuming from auto-pause, not a query problem.
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
| where type has "SQL"
| summarize
    calls = count(),
    failed = countif(success == false),
    median = percentile(duration, 50),
    p95 = percentile(duration, 95)
  by target, name
| order by calls desc
